      "keyInsight": "Here is the great trick your mind plays on you: severe physical pain can be completely real without any physical damage. Your brain acts like a nervous building manager hearing a terrifying alarm in the basement. Instead of facing the real crisis\u2014deep, messy emotional stress like anger, pressure, or guilt\u2014it pulls the fire alarm in your lower back or neck. Why? Because a physical ache is easy to understand. You can ice it, rest it, and blame your office chair. You obsess over spinal scans while the scary feelings stay locked safely underground. The pain is not imaginary. The spasm is genuine. But the target is a trick. Your brain stages a fake emergency to keep your conscious mind busy. Once you see the scam, the alarm loses its power, and the pain mysteriously evaporates.",
      "content": "Imagine your body is a high-tech car with a nervous computer system. Deep inside the engine, tension builds up from endless highway driving and poor maintenance. But instead of showing an engine warning, the dashboard flashes a flat tire alert. You pull over, inspect the rubber, and swap tires repeatedly. Yet the car still rattles. That is exactly how psychosomatic medicine works. Physical symptoms like burning back pain, stiff tendons, and sudden spasms are real bodily events. But their actual fuel is emotional pressure. Your brain slightly throttles blood flow to certain muscles, cutting off tiny amounts of oxygen. The result is intense, genuine pain that grabs all your attention.\n\nWhy would your own body pull such a nasty prank on you? Think of it as a magician waving a bright red handkerchief in his right hand. You watch the bright cloth intently while his left hand slips a coin into his pocket. The pain is that bright red cloth. Your brain hates messy, dangerous feelings like fury, resentment, and unbearable pressure. It considers them too explosive for daily life. So it stages a physical drama instead. As long as you worry about your spine, your posture, or your mattress, you never have to face the emotional storm brewing underneath.\n\nDoctors often get trapped in the magician's illusion too. They look at pictures of normal wear and tear on your spine and declare it a crime scene. But gray hair on your head does not cause a headache, and slight changes in your joints do not automatically create agony. When you treat a nervous system problem with endless pills, braces, and surgery, you are just polishing the dashboard warning light. Healing begins the moment you stop treating your body like cracked porcelain and start listening to what your nervous system is actually dodging.",
